The two protected wording passages that fall inside this movement are exact:

1. BOOK_MAP §8 item 22 appears in ch17 from “Brom. Iron Skin Path. We fight two weeks from today.” through “Good. Two weeks.” without a word changed.
2. BOOK_MAP §8 item 24 appears in ch21 exactly as “She's going to hit Silver-tier before she's done.” The manuscript immediately clarifies that Brom means a formal card, not the circuit ladder, preserving the Bronze-equivalent circuit ceiling.

Source reuse passes on the supplied result: **0 unprotected shared runs of eight or more words; 2 protected runs, allowed**. No reuse finding is raised. The referenced `source-overlap.tsv` was empty at review time, so this review relies on the supplied summary for the run count while independently verifying the two protected passages in the manuscript.

