editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/manuscript/chapter-20.md:47:Lira read it upside down and was quiet for a while.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/manuscript/chapter-20.md:63:For months there had been a line in the Pressure entry with nothing after it but a question. *Upper limit of the giving face under sustained use: not known.* He had never wanted to find it by going past it. He still had the second sprain in his left wrist in cold weather, and that had been an off-beat misfire, nothing like the top of anything; he had no wish at all to learn what the top felt like from the far side. So he did what he had done in the winter with Lira's stick. He did not go looking for the edge. He walked toward it a step at a time, slowly, and meant to stop as soon as he could see it.
